      {
        "nodeID": 1,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Sojourner Truth: That man over there says that women need to be helped into carriages, and lifted over ditches, and to have the best place everywhere"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 2,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "That Man: women need to be helped into carriages, and lifted over ditches, and to have the best place everywhere"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 3,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Sojourner Truth: Nobody ever helps me into carriages, or over mud-puddles, or gives me any best place"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 4,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Sojourner Truth: ain’t I a woman"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 5,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Sojourner Truth: Look at me! Look at my arm"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 6,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Sojourner Truth: I have ploughed and planted, and gathered into barns, and no man could head me"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 7,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Sojourner Truth: ain’t I a woman"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 8,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Sojourner Truth: I could work as much and eat as much as a man – when I could get it – and bear the lash as well"
      },
